.Dd April 9, 2026
.Dt TTY 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm tty
.Nd print the file name of the terminal connected to standard input
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl s
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The
.Nm
utility writes the file name of the terminal connected to standard input.
It first verifies that
.Dv STDIN_FILENO
refers to a terminal and then resolves the terminal name with
.Fn ttyname .
.Pp
If standard input is not a terminal,
.Nm
writes
.Dq not a tty
and exits with status 1.
.Pp
The options are as follows:
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl s
Suppress all output.
Only the exit status is significant.
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Ex -std tty
.Pp
The
.Nm
utility exits with one of the following values:
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It 0
Standard input is a terminal.
.It 1
Standard input is not a terminal.
.It 2
Usage error or terminal-name lookup failure.
.El
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr stty 1 ,
.Xr isatty 3 ,
.Xr ttyname 3
.Sh STANDARDS
The
.Nm
utility is expected to be IEEE Std 1003.1-2017
.Pq Dq POSIX.1
compatible.
